    <content>
        <subject>surveys</subject>
        <description>The Dark Energy Spectroscopic Instrument (DESI) is a 5-year spectroscopic redshift survey designed to map the three-dimensional structure of the universe between z=0 and z=4. Data Release 1 includes high-confidence redshifts for 18.7 million objects - 13.1 million galaxies, 1.6 million quasars, and 4 million stars - from observations taken between May 2021 and June 2022.</description>
        <referenceURL>https://data.desi.lbl.gov/doc/releases/dr1</referenceURL>
